@startuml fig-tester-container-lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Tester Container Lifecycle (entrypoint.sh)

participant "Docker Compose" as DC #E3F2FD
participant "entrypoint.sh" as EP #90CAF9
participant "tcpdump" as TD #C8E6C9
participant "Application\nServices" as APP #BBDEFB
participant "pytest" as PT #FFE0B2
participant "validate_pcap.py" as VP #E1BEE7

DC -> EP : start tester container\n(PROJECT_CODE set)

== PHASE 1 — CAPTURE ==

EP -> TD : tcpdump -i any -w traffic_e2.pcap &
activate TD #C8E6C9
EP -> EP : sleep 1, then check capture process\nexit 2 if capture failed to start

== PHASE 2 — SMOKE TESTS ==

EP -> PT : pytest -m e2
activate PT #FFE0B2
PT -> APP : HTTP / TCP / UDP requests
APP --> PT : responses
PT --> EP : exit code (TEST_RC)
deactivate PT

== PHASE 3 — STOP AND VALIDATE ==

EP -> TD : SIGINT, bounded wait\nTERM/KILL fallback; collect capture status
deactivate TD

EP -> VP : validate_pcap.py\n--project $PROJECT_CODE\n--pcap traffic_e2.pcap
activate VP #E1BEE7
VP --> EP : rule results (OK / FAIL)
deactivate VP

EP --> DC : preserve failing TEST_RC; otherwise\nexit 2 for capture failure or validator status

legend right
entrypoint.sh uses set -euo pipefail
for strict error handling.
Request SIGINT flush and inspect capture exit status.
Failed pytest still reaches cleanup and validation.
EXIT / INT / TERM traps perform bounded cleanup.
A passing capture check alone is not application acceptance.
endlegend
@enduml
